In the past decades the 3GPP organization never stopped to grow while the methods and tools used for managing CRs and TSs/TRs remained unchanged. Today, the ever-increasing number of contributions and CRs, and the large sizes of our TSs/TRs reveal more than ever the shortcomings of the tools we are currently using. The top 3 of these short comes are: manual implementation of the CRs, browsing large TSs files, writing/checking proper ASN.1 code. In this contribution we take a close look at each one of the above-mentioned shortcomings and we try to foresee possible solutions to overcome them.

